, {"t": " disables", "lp": -0.8176041841506958, "top": [[" disables", -0.8176041841506958], [" explicitly", -1.7325536012649536]]}, {"t": " `", "lp": -1.1629862785339355, "top": [[" c", -0.9984182715415955], [" `", -1.1629862785339355]]}, {"t": "cc", "lp": -0.009588166140019894, "top": [["cc", -0.009588166140019894], ["nc", -5.96501350402832]]}, {"t": "ache", "lp": -0.000784704927355051, "top": [["ache", -0.000784704927355051], ["ACHE", -8.682470321655273]]}, {"t": "`", "lp": -0.4286736249923706, "top": [["`", -0.4286736249923706], ["`.", -1.0824861526489258]]}, {"t": "/", "lp": -0.035750746726989746, "top": [["/", -0.035750746726989746], [" (", -3.9100029468536377]]}, {"t": "`", "lp": -0.08511862903833389, "top": [["`", -0.08511862903833389], ["s", -3.6100380420684814]]}], "text": "# PKGBUILD build() Function \u2014 Step by Step\n\nLet me break down this `build()` function line by line, explaining each flag and its purpose.\n\n## The Setup\n\n```bash\nsource /opt/intel/oneapi/setvars.sh --force\n```\nThis loads the Intel oneAPI environment variables (PATH, library paths, compiler locations) so that `icx`/`icpx` are available. The `--force` flag makes it reconfigure the environment in the current shell rather than spawning a subshell.\n\n```bash\nset -e\n```\nStops the script immediately if any command exits with a non-zero status.\n\n## The CMake Invocation\n\n```bash\ncmake -S \"${srcdir}/llama.cpp\" -B \"${srcdir}/build\" -G Ninja\n```\n- `-S` \u2014 source directory (the cloned repo)\n- `-B` \u2014 build directory\n- `-G Ninja` \u2014 use the Ninja build generator (fast, minimal output)\n\n## Build Type & Installation\n\n```bash\n-DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release\n```\nOptimized build with `-O3`-level optimizations (but note `!debug` option prevents `-g` flags).\n\n```bash\n-DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/usr -DCMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR=lib\n```\nInstalls binaries to `/usr` and libraries to `/usr/lib`.\n\n## Compilers\n\n```bash\n-DCMAKE_C_COMPILER=icx -DCMAKE_CXX_COMPILER=icpx\n```\nUse Intel's DPC++/ICX compilers (C and C++) instead of GCC \u2014 required for SYCL GPU support.\n\n```bash\n-DCMAKE_C_COMPILER_LAUNCHER= -DCMAKE_CXX_COMPILER_LAUNCHER=\n```\n**Empty launchers** \u2014 this disables `ccache`/`"}